Ours (dsv41 recipe), Apache-2.0, against vLLM main 6e517b15 + patches 0001-0021.
Calibrated confidences for the DSpark verify depth (patch 0010), and a per-round log to fit them from; both off by
default. The DSpark paper (arXiv 2607.05147, section 3.2.1) calibrates its confidence head per position with
temperature scaling before the scheduler forms prefix survivals (its raw head: ECE 3-8%, ~1% calibrated); DeepSeek's
checkpoint ships no temperatures, so 0010 reads the raw scores.
VLLM_DSPARK_CONF_TEMPS="t1,...,tk" (one value covers every position, a short list repeats its last value) and
VLLM_DSPARK_CONF_BIAS="b1,...,bk" (default 0): the conf rule reads sigmoid(logit(c_i) / t_i + b_i) in place of c_i.
The head is one fp32 Linear(hidden + Markov rank -> 1) and vLLM keeps sigmoid of its logit
(draft_token_confidence_probs, fp32), so the policy takes torch.logit of that (clamped 1e-6 from 0 and 1) outside the
captured draft graph: the temperature on the head's logit, to fp32 rounding. Only the depth moves, and rows up to any
depth compute what the full window computes for them (0010), so greedy text does not change.
VLLM_DSPARK_CONF_LOG=<path.jsonl> (+ VLLM_DSPARK_CONF_LOG_TAG, a run tag for the header): rank 0 appends a header line
(k, policy, cost table, temperatures) at start and whenever VLLM_DSPARK_DEPTH_FILE changes the policy or the table,
then one line per request per verify round: request id, step, the raw confidences (before any temperature), the depth
that round used, the drafts in the window and the drafts accepted. Confidences are kept by request slot when drafted
and joined with the acceptance after the next verify; each step's rows take one async copy into a pinned 8-slot ring
and are written once their event has completed, so a step waits on the GPU only if all 8 slots are still in flight
(~0.1 ms of host time a step with the log on). The logged id contains the client's X-Request-Id, so a tag there names
the domain. Fit from a log taken under VLLM_DSPARK_DEPTH_POLICY=fixed:<k>: every position is then verified whenever
its prefix survives, with no selection by the scores being fitted. Test: patches/tests/test_dspark_conf_calibration.py.

